              "content": "={{ $json.text }}"
            },
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are extracting structured data from raw text pulled from an invoice PDF. The text may have labels and values in a different order than they appear on the printed page, because it was extracted from the PDF's layout rather than its visual reading order. Do not assume a value immediately follows its label in the text.\n\nExtract exactly three fields:\n\n1. invoice_id — The invoice number, always in the format INV-XX-#### (e.g., INV-AC-1001). Search the full text for a string matching this pattern; do not use any other number (dates, amounts, quantities) as the invoice ID.\n2. vendor — The company that issued the invoice and is requesting payment. This is NOT the company listed under \"Bill To\" — \"Bill To\" always refers to the customer being billed, never the vendor. The vendor name typically appears near the top of the document, separate from the \"Bill To\" section. If the vendor field is missing, blank, or contains only a placeholder character (such as a single period, dash, or \"N/A\") with no real company name, return null for this field — do not treat a placeholder as a valid vendor name.\n3. amount — The final total amount owed on the invoice, often labeled \"Total,\" \"Balance Due,\" or similar. If multiple dollar figures appear (e.g., subtotal, tax, and total), use the final total — the largest figure that represents subtotal + tax, not the subtotal alone or the tax alone.\n\nReturn your answer as strict JSON only, with no preamble, no explanation, and no markdown formatting — just the raw JSON object, in exactly this shape:\n{\"invoice_id\": \"string or null\", \"vendor\": \"string or null\", \"amount\": number or null}\n\nExample 1:\nInput text: INVOICE\\n# INV-AC-1001\\nAcme Supplies\\nBill To:\\nNorthgate Retail Ltd\\nAug 1, 2026\\nAug 31, 2026\\n$450.00\\nDate:\\nDue Date:\\nBalance Due:\\nItem Quantity Rate Amount\\nOffice Supplies Restock 1 $450.00 $450.00\\n$450.00\\n$0.00\\n$450.00\\nSubtotal:\\nTax (0%):\\nTotal:\n\nOutput: {\"invoice_id\": \"INV-AC-1001\", \"vendor\": \"Acme Supplies\", \"amount\": 450.00}\n\nExample 2:\nInput text: INVOICE\\n# INV-BR-3007\\n.\\nBill To:\\nNorthgate Retail Ltd\\nAug 10, 2026\\nAug 31, 2026\\n$150.00\\nDate:\\nDue Date:\\nBalance Due:\\nItem Quantity Rate Amount\\nOffice Cleaning Service 1 $150.00 $150.00\\n$150.00\\n$0.00\\n$150.00\\nSubtotal:\\nTax (0%):\\nTotal:\n\nOutput: {\"invoice_id\": \"INV-BR-3007\", \"vendor\": null, \"amount\": 150.00}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
